# solar_hourly_event.te — TE-Probes-Wanderung: the solar_hourly_event_probe pair over registered fields.
# driver: GOES XRS-A channel, goes_xrs_xrsa (phi/sources.φ:832, goes_xrs.bin, 3600 s).
#   solar_hourly_event_probe.rs:537-547 actor 0 "XRSA"; the first actor pair (:640-648).
# target: GOES XRS-B channel, goes_xrs_xrsb (phi/sources.φ:833). solar_hourly_event_probe.rs
#   :548-557 actor 1 "XRSB".
# The probe is an event-wise all-actor matrix over 2013-2015 (11 actors, 110 directed pairs x
#   8 lags; solar_hourly_event_probe.rs:480-509, :640-680); field_te_query carries one
#   driver/target pair, so this descriptor names the first pair, the remaining directed pairs
#   stay the probe's own matrix.
# cond: none — the flare events (GOES b_flux > 5e-6 W/m^2, :490) feed an event stack, not a
#   cond arm.
# cadence: hourly cells (solar_hourly_event_probe.rs:17 HOUR 3600.0; :18 LAGS_HOUR 0..7;
#   :20 N_SURR 10).
pair solar-hourly-event
register sources
driver goes_xrs_xrsa
target goes_xrs_xrsb
cadence live
bin 3600
seasonal none
lags 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7
surrogate 10
